// Statement recovery resynchronizes past a `{ … }` group the failed statement itself opened, so a
// later statement's fault is still found. Recovery skips a BALANCED group whole; stopping at its
// closing `}` instead parks on a brace nothing can consume, and every following statement is
// silently swallowed. `}` still means "the enclosing block ends here" — that is what keeps a bad
// statement inside a block from running past the block.
// expect: error E0003 at 10:7
// expect: error E0003 at 11:6
// expect: error E0003 at 12:8
// expect: exit 1
x = { "a" };
echo ;
y = [{ f() }];
